WEBVTT

00:01.716 --> 00:03.926
It's almost here…
The old man's ship.

00:04.052 --> 00:05.595
Right on time.

00:05.887 --> 00:07.346
He's about twenty minutes away.

00:07.472 --> 00:10.683
I-Is Mr. Joseph Joestar
the only passenger?

00:11.059 --> 00:11.851
Yeah.

00:12.102 --> 00:15.605
The rest of the crew is made up of
folks from the Speedwagon Foundation.

00:16.231 --> 00:20.731
Chili Pepper may be
confined to areas of electricity,

00:20.902 --> 00:23.404
but I'm sure that
won't stop him from trying to

00:23.488 --> 00:25.615
pass over the water and
onto the old man's ship.

00:25.991 --> 00:30.328
If he gets to him first, we lose.

00:31.037 --> 00:32.121
He'll kill the old man.

00:32.831 --> 00:33.706
Jotaro!

00:33.957 --> 00:36.000
The boat looks good.

00:36.251 --> 00:37.418
As far as the battery goes,

00:38.003 --> 00:39.504
he's not hiding in there.

00:39.588 --> 00:41.965
We're all clear and ready to go.

00:42.174 --> 00:43.049
Josuke…

00:43.425 --> 00:46.094
Okuyasu and I are the only ones
heading to meet the old man.

00:46.219 --> 00:46.969
Huh?

00:47.304 --> 00:50.307
You will hold the fort here
with Koichi.

00:50.432 --> 00:52.934
Stay here?! With Josuke?

00:53.185 --> 00:54.186
Why?

00:54.603 --> 00:58.732
Josuke, Chili Pepper's user is hiding
somewhere here in this harbor,

00:58.815 --> 01:00.066
watching us.

01:01.318 --> 01:03.486
He's waiting for us to make our move,

01:04.070 --> 01:06.489
so he can confirm the boat's position.

01:08.658 --> 01:12.036
And my hunch is he won't be
hiding on a boat.

01:12.370 --> 01:16.791
All he needs is a battery and
something faster than a motorboat.

01:17.584 --> 01:19.293
Just like the bike,

01:17.667 --> 01:22.167
PORT OF MORIOH

01:19.503 --> 01:22.756
he'll find something with a battery and
send Chili Pepper flying on that.

01:22.881 --> 01:22.944
Flying? You mean up in the sky?

01:25.967 --> 01:26.717
Yeah.

01:26.927 --> 01:28.386
I wouldn't be surprised if Chili Pepper

01:28.803 --> 01:31.972
was making off with
a remote-controlled plane as we speak.

01:32.432 --> 01:34.559
A remote-controlled airplane?!

01:34.935 --> 01:36.102
It's possible!

01:36.186 --> 01:40.440
Once they pick up speed,
model airplanes can fly over 100 kph!

01:40.524 --> 01:42.692
That's faster than this motorboat.

01:43.026 --> 01:45.194
And because
Chili Pepper's controlling it,

01:45.278 --> 01:48.698
he can fly as far and as high as
the battery will take him!

01:49.324 --> 01:51.451
He doesn't need
a remote control's signal!

01:51.660 --> 01:54.454
Josuke, if you spot anything
flying around here,

01:54.538 --> 01:56.623
I want you to search for his user.

01:57.165 --> 01:59.709
Koichi's Reverb has
a range of fifty meters.

01:59.876 --> 02:01.210
He can help.

02:02.671 --> 02:06.299
If he beats us to the punch,
the old man is done for.

02:07.008 --> 02:10.011
You will safeguard your father
from terra firm a!

02:10.178 --> 02:11.637
Understand, Josuke?

02:12.347 --> 02:16.847
Yeah, I'm well aware
we don't have a second to spare.

02:33.535 --> 02:35.954
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

02:37.247 --> 02:40.583
<i>These faceless gazes pass by one another</i>

02:40.917 --> 02:44.253
<i>A wound to the heart changes our everyday</i>

02:44.462 --> 02:48.962
<i>Encounters without boundaries
The bizarre is our normal U-yeh</i>

02:51.428 --> 02:54.764
<i>These ordinary mornings,
we're laughing on the surface</i>

02:54.848 --> 02:58.476
<i>Mysteries drawn to each other,
identity still unknown</i>

02:58.560 --> 03:03.060
<i>Without a heads up,
it's quietly lurking somewhere in this town</i>

03:07.652 --> 03:12.152
<i>Although we bicker and complain
In the end, we celebrate</i>

03:14.701 --> 03:18.079
<i>Dancing through the everyday</i>

03:18.163 --> 03:22.663
<i>Crazy Noisy Bizarre Town</i>

03:34.554 --> 03:39.054
EPISODE 12
CHILI PEPPER, PART 2

03:38.266 --> 03:39.246
Good luck, Okuyasu.

03:44.648 --> 03:46.650
Thanks, Koichi.

04:01.956 --> 04:03.290
In just about twenty minutes,

04:03.375 --> 04:06.336
we'll arrive at
the Port of Morioh, Mr. Joestar.

04:08.129 --> 04:11.340
Is that so? Uh…

04:11.925 --> 04:15.386
Would you happen to know
where my cane is?

04:15.804 --> 04:18.765
Um, isn't that it right there
in front of you?

04:19.766 --> 04:21.100
Ahh…

04:28.108 --> 04:29.859
My own father, huh…

04:32.904 --> 04:34.989
Josuke? Are you all right?

04:37.409 --> 04:41.909
Out of the blue, I'm told a man
I've never met is my father…

04:44.165 --> 04:45.291
It's… I don't know…

04:53.508 --> 04:57.386
But, his life's in danger.

04:57.637 --> 05:00.681
Not doing everything I can
would haunt my dreams forever.

05:01.182 --> 05:04.393
Besides, my mom would break down in
a puddle of tears if he ever bit the dust.

05:06.396 --> 05:08.481
Damn! It must've been Jotaro!

05:08.690 --> 05:12.193
If he left you two behind
to sniff out my user…

05:13.027 --> 05:17.527
Then he completely saw through
my remote-controlled plane trick!

05:18.825 --> 05:20.451
Chili Pepper!

05:20.952 --> 05:22.078
Yeah!

05:25.540 --> 05:29.168
Jotaro Kujo is sharp as a tack.

05:32.213 --> 05:35.591
And he's the last person
I want finding me.

05:37.051 --> 05:39.845
This remote-controlled Spitfire plane

05:39.971 --> 05:43.391
can reach Joseph Joestar's boat
in a mere five minutes.

05:43.933 --> 05:48.433
A motorboat, on the other hand,
will take about eight to ten.

05:49.022 --> 05:52.358
Meaning, if I put the two
of you down in about three minutes,

05:52.484 --> 05:54.736
I can catch up and
pass them with time to spare.

05:55.069 --> 05:57.613
Y-You're Chili Pepper's user?

05:58.072 --> 06:00.949
You're looking at Akira Otoishi,
age nineteen.

06:01.075 --> 06:03.827
Oh, and don't mind this guitar.

06:05.580 --> 06:10.080
One day, I want to be
an ultra super guitarist

06:10.627 --> 06:15.127
who lives hard and fast,
just like Jimi Hendrix and Jeff Beck!

06:16.299 --> 06:19.552
That's why I keep
this baby on me at all times!

06:20.011 --> 06:23.848
And before you know it,
I'm gonna be knocking out…

06:28.394 --> 06:31.105
people all over the world
with this guitar!

06:31.189 --> 06:32.607
Oh, yeah.

06:34.275 --> 06:35.818
I never would've thought.

06:36.110 --> 06:38.695
A Stand user out in the open.

06:39.280 --> 06:41.657
Which means,
there's not a doubt in his mind

06:41.741 --> 06:44.160
that he can slaughter
Josuke and me both!

06:44.452 --> 06:47.413
YEEEES

06:47.455 --> 06:51.955
Against your Shining Diamond,
I'll use nothing but my little ol' pinky,

06:52.418 --> 06:54.420
just like I did with Okuyasu.

06:54.879 --> 06:56.171
Get back, Koichi.

06:59.634 --> 07:01.636
It's game on, Josuke Higashikata!

07:01.803 --> 07:02.720
One sec, please.

07:02.804 --> 07:03.554
Huh?

07:03.888 --> 07:06.515
If you're going to use only your pinky,

07:06.766 --> 07:08.392
then I've got some rules, too.

07:08.476 --> 07:10.853
Rules? You better learn some respect!

07:11.145 --> 07:14.106
Rules are wasted on a punk like you!

07:16.985 --> 07:19.696
How dare you, you bastard?!

07:19.863 --> 07:22.282
Well, you said rules are wasted on me.

07:22.448 --> 07:25.951
Weren't you saying something about
bringing me down with your little pinky?

07:26.077 --> 07:27.495
So what'll it be,

07:27.662 --> 07:29.413
big-shot senior, Otoishi?

07:29.497 --> 07:30.831
I'm gonna destroy you.

07:30.957 --> 07:32.541
You already said that!

07:32.667 --> 07:34.960
You can stop
repeating yourself, dumb-ass!

07:36.588 --> 07:38.631
The pain, the agony…

07:38.715 --> 07:41.050
I must redirect it onto something!

07:42.677 --> 07:44.387
This rage…

07:44.512 --> 07:47.181
I have to vent to someone!

08:12.707 --> 08:13.749
He's amazing…

08:18.171 --> 08:20.006
RIGHT-HAND TAPPING

08:20.089 --> 08:21.882
I'M GOING TO KILL

08:21.966 --> 08:26.261
YOUR MOMMIES, TOO!

08:29.557 --> 08:32.768
I just set my heart free!

08:32.894 --> 08:36.856
I just let that blistering rage fly.

08:37.565 --> 08:40.901
Try me, Otoishi!

08:44.072 --> 08:46.199
Wh-What? The user just…

08:47.283 --> 08:49.910
I know Stands can move
at incredible speed,

08:50.244 --> 08:53.997
but a user bolting behind me?

08:54.457 --> 08:56.083
Th-That's not it, Josuke!

08:56.417 --> 08:58.627
I saw everything from back here!

08:58.753 --> 09:01.005
Otoishi didn't move…

09:01.130 --> 09:03.298
The one who moved was you!

09:03.466 --> 09:04.717
Something moved you!

09:04.801 --> 09:05.551
What?

09:05.927 --> 09:09.138
Chili Pepper appeared and
flipped Shining Diamond

09:09.389 --> 09:11.474
around 180 degrees in a flash!

09:12.600 --> 09:14.893
You're facing the ocean, aren't you?

09:15.478 --> 09:17.480
Chili Pepper appeared?

09:18.523 --> 09:21.984
Koichi! I haven't seen
that bastard Chili Pepper anywhere!

09:22.276 --> 09:23.610
He's underground!

09:23.736 --> 09:25.654
Look at all the storm drains!

09:27.407 --> 09:29.826
He poked himself halfway
out of the drain just now!

09:29.951 --> 09:32.620
There must be electrical lines
running all over under there!

09:32.954 --> 09:37.041
A little soul-searching
always fires me up.

09:37.208 --> 09:38.834
Behind you on your right!

09:45.174 --> 09:46.800
Now he's right behind you!

09:55.601 --> 09:58.437
He keeps bolting back into
the electrical wires at the last second!

09:58.521 --> 10:00.356
And at light speed!

10:00.481 --> 10:03.275
Jotaro's the only one
who can keep up!

10:03.484 --> 10:05.652
You don't have the luxury
of digging up the asphalt

10:05.778 --> 10:09.490
and severing the wires,
Josuke Higashikata.

10:09.615 --> 10:13.702
And the bigger the opening you make…

10:14.495 --> 10:17.623
the easier it is for me
to surface from below!

10:17.957 --> 10:19.291
Josuke! To your right!

10:19.834 --> 10:20.876
In front of you!

10:21.335 --> 10:22.210
Behind you!

10:22.587 --> 10:24.547
No, wait! Um…

10:27.008 --> 10:29.010
It's like super expert level
whack-a-mole!

10:29.093 --> 10:31.845
I can't follow his movements
at that speed!

10:35.433 --> 10:38.436
Guessing really isn't going
to get you anywhere!

10:40.938 --> 10:42.230
Josuke…

10:42.690 --> 10:45.067
And I still have two minutes left…

10:45.234 --> 10:47.486
That's plenty of time
to do away with you.

10:50.990 --> 10:54.827
Koichi, watch for Chili Pepper's
location and report it me.

10:55.078 --> 10:58.456
I'm too close to tell!

10:58.539 --> 11:00.749
I-I can't tell, either!

11:00.875 --> 11:02.877
Just when I think he's out,
he goes back in!

11:02.960 --> 11:04.878
Look harder, Koichi.

11:05.505 --> 11:09.091
You should be able to tell
what I'm thinking by now.

11:09.550 --> 11:11.301
Huh? What you're thinking?

11:14.931 --> 11:16.515
<i>I-It's all squishy!</i>

11:16.849 --> 11:18.725
<i>The asphalt's turned into tar…</i>

11:19.102 --> 11:22.021
<i>The drains are covered
in oil from the tar!</i>

11:22.688 --> 11:23.438
<i>I get it!</i>

11:23.564 --> 11:25.232
<i>When he struck the ground,</i>

11:25.399 --> 11:28.276
<i>he reduced the asphalt to
its most basic ingredients!</i>

11:28.611 --> 11:29.361
<i>Which means…</i>

11:31.614 --> 11:33.532
Behind you, to your left!

11:37.120 --> 11:39.455
Yeah! Bull's eye!

11:40.414 --> 11:43.542
Bull's eye? That's great.

11:44.210 --> 11:46.128
Do I get a prize

11:46.212 --> 11:48.631
if I smack him around some more?

11:52.802 --> 11:55.554
CHILI PEPPER

11:58.975 --> 11:59.725
It's the boat!

11:59.809 --> 12:01.811
We're close enough
I can read its number!

12:01.936 --> 12:03.604
W-We're almost there!

12:03.729 --> 12:04.980
Don't let your guard down yet.

12:05.106 --> 12:05.856
Huh?

12:06.149 --> 12:08.234
Wh-What the hell is that?

12:08.943 --> 12:11.362
Josuke! Koichi!

12:13.781 --> 12:15.157
That light!

12:15.283 --> 12:19.783
It seems I didn't take you nearly
serious enough, Josuke Higashikata.

12:22.456 --> 12:25.667
I should lose my juvenile thinking,

12:25.793 --> 12:28.086
shouldn't I?

12:29.255 --> 12:33.755
I'm focusing all of Morioh's
electricity into Chili Pepper!

12:34.218 --> 12:35.844
I'm only doing this now

12:35.970 --> 12:40.470
because it temporarily
reduces my power source,

12:41.142 --> 12:43.144
this entire region's electricity,
to nothing!

12:43.644 --> 12:45.437
But I don't care anymore!

12:45.563 --> 12:49.984
After I crush you fools, all I have to do
is use the RC plane's battery

12:50.109 --> 12:53.070
to fly to Joseph and kill him!

12:54.322 --> 12:56.365
I-I can't see!

12:58.075 --> 12:59.826
You bastard…

13:13.216 --> 13:16.677
He totally overwhelmed Josuke!

13:20.932 --> 13:22.516
Josuke!

13:26.145 --> 13:27.521
Don't you see?

13:27.647 --> 13:30.650
This entire town's electrical power
is at my disposal!

13:32.151 --> 13:34.987
I'll be sure to tack on
my entire electric bill

13:35.071 --> 13:36.781
onto your meter.

13:39.700 --> 13:42.577
It's lights out, Josuke!

13:46.082 --> 13:46.832
Is this a tire?!

13:50.461 --> 13:54.006
By the time you figure it out,
it'll be way too late.

13:56.717 --> 13:59.594
You blew up that tire
on purpose, didn't you?

13:59.762 --> 14:02.890
It was all to entomb
my Stand in rubber!

14:03.015 --> 14:06.768
Of course! Tire rubber is an insulator,
so it doesn't conduct electricity!

14:06.894 --> 14:08.979
Chili Pepper can't use electricity!

14:09.063 --> 14:10.773
Dammit!

14:10.898 --> 14:13.275
Yes! Now we just have
to wait for Jotaro…

14:13.567 --> 14:14.776
Just kidding.

14:14.860 --> 14:15.652
Huh?

14:15.903 --> 14:18.363
So you think you can insulate
me with rubber?

14:19.323 --> 14:22.284
Maybe it would've worked
if it had been a meter thick!

14:22.410 --> 14:23.619
Don't make me laugh!

14:23.744 --> 14:27.622
Like this flimsy rubber
could've done anything!

14:27.748 --> 14:29.583
Dummy!

14:32.712 --> 14:35.131
You've lost, Josuke!

14:37.341 --> 14:40.510
Great. You'd be a lot better off

14:41.095 --> 14:44.681
if you hadn't had the strength
to break through that tire.

14:48.227 --> 14:50.103
Th-The air in the tire!

14:50.187 --> 14:52.772
It was completely full?!

14:57.778 --> 15:01.114
N-Not the ocean! Anything but that!

15:01.240 --> 15:03.158
O-Oh, yeah…

15:03.284 --> 15:06.328
<i>Salt water conducts electricity</i>

15:06.412 --> 15:09.998
<i>The vastness of the ocean means
the electricity scatters in every direction!</i>

15:10.082 --> 15:12.375
I'm sorry! Please!

15:12.460 --> 15:14.170
- Get me out of here!
- You said something about

15:14.253 --> 15:17.214
wanting to lose your juvenile thinking.

15:17.298 --> 15:20.843
But that, my friend,
is a permanent character flaw.

15:25.765 --> 15:28.517
I-I'm dissolving…

15:30.561 --> 15:33.772
His Stand's been diffused!
Which means…

15:40.196 --> 15:42.656
H-He's dead?

15:48.204 --> 15:49.997
Jotaro!

15:50.456 --> 15:52.249
We defeated the user!

15:52.500 --> 15:55.002
We defeated Chili Pepper's user!

15:55.127 --> 15:57.420
Well done.
We can all breathe a little easier.

15:58.756 --> 16:02.259
<i>So this is Josuke's dad..</i>

16:02.718 --> 16:07.218
<i>He looks huge, but the geezer
looks like he's on his last legs.</i>

16:09.725 --> 16:11.727
You there,

16:11.977 --> 16:14.354
what's your name?

16:14.605 --> 16:15.939
Okuyasu.

16:16.148 --> 16:17.357
Okuyasu?

16:17.483 --> 16:20.611
I live in Josuke's neighborhood;
I'm a Stand user, too.

16:20.694 --> 16:21.486
Huh?

16:21.737 --> 16:23.071
A Stand user.

16:23.197 --> 16:23.947
Huh?

16:24.532 --> 16:26.742
A S-t-a-n-d u-s-e-r!

16:26.867 --> 16:29.703
Ah, you bought
a second-hand computer?

16:29.787 --> 16:31.079
I'm a Stand user!

16:31.205 --> 16:34.708
Oh, is that it?!
You're a Stand user.

16:34.792 --> 16:36.418
It's no picnic.

16:36.585 --> 16:38.211
By the way, Osomatsu,

16:38.337 --> 16:42.299
I can't seem to find my cane.
Do you know where it is?

16:43.884 --> 16:44.718
Ah!

16:45.052 --> 16:48.513
Oh silly me.
I'm holding it here in my hand.

16:48.597 --> 16:50.765
<i>Is this old-timer okay?</i>

16:51.892 --> 16:53.101
Mr. Joestar.

16:54.437 --> 16:56.147
I've come to pick up your luggage.

16:57.815 --> 17:01.360
By the way, Osomatsu,
I'd like to know.

17:02.820 --> 17:05.113
Has Josuke mentioned me?

17:05.573 --> 17:09.952
The man who for sixteen years
didn't know he was born…

17:10.453 --> 17:12.621
Has he said anything at all?

17:13.998 --> 17:17.876
Can't say he's said much about that.

17:18.461 --> 17:22.548
Is that so. So he hasn't…

17:24.091 --> 17:26.510
Yay! They're finally here!

17:26.677 --> 17:28.470
Look, Josuke!

17:28.554 --> 17:30.973
Oh, that's good news, I guess.

17:32.308 --> 17:34.310
To be honest,

17:34.727 --> 17:37.646
I kinda wish he'd just go back home.

17:38.147 --> 17:39.314
Josuke…

17:39.482 --> 17:43.652
Well, I am glad Otoishi didn't kill him.

17:43.944 --> 17:45.654
Now everyone can
live happily ever after.

17:46.197 --> 17:47.698
But you know…

17:48.782 --> 17:51.868
I've never even met him.

17:52.203 --> 17:54.955
How can I think of him as my dad?

17:56.040 --> 17:59.293
It's gonna be totally awkward
for both of us.

18:01.212 --> 18:03.589
It's not like I hate him or anything.

18:04.215 --> 18:06.425
But I have to think about my mom, too.

18:07.760 --> 18:10.179
Don't you think, Koichi?

18:11.222 --> 18:12.973
O-Oh, no…

18:13.807 --> 18:15.683
Josuke, more trouble!

18:15.809 --> 18:17.936
H-His body!

18:20.231 --> 18:22.107
Jotaro, we're in big trouble!

18:22.233 --> 18:24.443
Akira Otoishi's body is gone!

18:25.611 --> 18:26.528
He's still

18:27.154 --> 18:28.196
alive!

18:28.906 --> 18:31.283
Bad news!
The enemy has infiltrated our ship!

18:31.909 --> 18:33.827
Akira Otoishi is still alive!

18:33.953 --> 18:35.079
Are you kidding?

18:35.162 --> 18:36.413
Take Mr. Joestar…

18:38.832 --> 18:39.916
Who are you?

18:40.834 --> 18:42.836
Huh? Did you say something?

18:43.337 --> 18:44.713
No, he…

18:44.797 --> 18:46.381
I said it!

18:46.465 --> 18:49.468
He's not from
the Speedwagon Foundation!

18:49.593 --> 18:50.093
Wha…

18:50.177 --> 18:51.469
What?!

18:51.679 --> 18:52.513
He's the enemy!

18:52.680 --> 18:54.390
You sure 'bout that? Bastard!

18:54.515 --> 18:55.933
Wait!

18:56.058 --> 18:58.685
I'm the one who told you
about the enemy!

18:58.769 --> 19:00.854
Would any enemy do that?!

19:01.981 --> 19:03.107
This man is the enemy!

19:03.232 --> 19:04.316
He's got a point!

19:04.400 --> 19:07.444
I pointed out the enemy
in the first place!

19:07.611 --> 19:10.238
He came here to
throw you off your guard!

19:10.364 --> 19:11.907
He's got a point, too…

19:12.032 --> 19:15.243
Wh-Who's the user?

19:15.369 --> 19:16.453
- He is!
- He is!

19:16.579 --> 19:17.454
<i>Dammit!</i>

19:17.621 --> 19:19.789
<i>Another decision?</i>

19:19.873 --> 19:20.832
<i>Goddammit.</i>

19:21.041 --> 19:24.044
<i>This is what I get
for relying on Bro my whole life…</i>

19:24.295 --> 19:26.714
<i>Okuyasu'll be easy to dispose of</i>

19:26.797 --> 19:29.758
<i>And Jotaro hasn't seen my face yet.</i>

19:29.842 --> 19:32.010
<i>As long as I kill Joseph…</i>

19:33.220 --> 19:34.512
<i>I'll get out of here!</i>

19:34.680 --> 19:36.264
<i>They'll never catch me!</i>

19:36.390 --> 19:38.225
Chili Pepper!

19:38.475 --> 19:41.728
Huh? What's that about
a smelly setter?

19:43.731 --> 19:44.857
Time to die!

19:55.409 --> 19:57.327
I figured out!

19:57.578 --> 19:59.288
The user is…

19:59.413 --> 20:02.290
You!

20:09.340 --> 20:13.840
Nobody fools Okuyasu Nijimura twice!

20:14.720 --> 20:18.181
H-How'd you know?

20:18.724 --> 20:19.850
You wanna know?

20:20.309 --> 20:21.393
How…

20:22.186 --> 20:25.314
I was gonna beat
the shit out of you both!

20:25.606 --> 20:27.899
I'm not too smart, you know.

21:02.768 --> 21:04.060
Watch…

21:04.895 --> 21:08.023
your step.
You'll fall in the water.

21:08.148 --> 21:10.358
S-Sorry.

21:10.651 --> 21:13.528
If I had my cane,
I could manage by myself.

21:14.488 --> 21:17.699
But it broke a moment ago…

21:18.033 --> 21:20.618
G-Guess I don't have a choice.

21:22.121 --> 21:24.873
Grab my hand.

21:42.975 --> 21:45.143
I just had a great idea!

21:45.269 --> 21:47.771
If Shining Diamond fixes the cane…

21:47.896 --> 21:50.189
Y-You dolt! What are you saying?

21:50.357 --> 21:52.525
That was really dumb, Okuyasu!

21:52.651 --> 21:54.069
Huh? Why?

21:54.653 --> 21:59.153
'Cause this is one time leaving it
broken is better.

22:01.493 --> 22:03.369
Huh? Why?

22:03.871 --> 22:04.746
Why is that?

22:06.457 --> 22:09.918
<i>Now if we can just take back
the bow and arrow, it'll all be over…</i>

22:11.170 --> 22:12.754
<i>Not to mention,
this town'll be safe.</i>

23:38.799 --> 23:42.010
EPISODE 13
WE PICKED UP SOMETHING CRAZY!
